{
  "date": "2026-10-19",
  "base_commit": "810c20fbc806861a3a21c4f191eebb585453bf74",
  "scope": "Two existing research drafts updated; promoted main papers and Lean sources unchanged.",
  "new_results": [
    "Exact-anchor compression: a critical variational path of action A0 and square-root entropy S has a same-depth tanh realization with width at most C(d+L+A0)^30 exp(20S) and uniform output error at most 3/32.",
    "Critical-rate sublevel capacity: log cardinality at rate at most a is bounded by a universal polynomial in d,L,a+2 times exp(C sqrt(L(a-V*)_+)).",
    "Actual critical posterior learning at all sufficiently large widths, including tied-rate mixtures, with the resulting sample bound and a sample-independent but unquantified width threshold.",
    "Polynomial sample complexity for every parity at L >= C log(d+L+2), and more generally polynomial dependence on Fourier variation under the stated depth condition.",
    "For bounded-weight teachers of depth D, sufficient sample size R^{O(D+1)} at L >= C(D+1)log R: polynomial learner-depth dependence for fixed teacher depth.",
    "Depth-independent product-cost bounds for editing finitely many Boolean labels and multiplying by a low-Fourier-variation predicate."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "A sample bound jointly polynomial in arbitrary teacher width and depth remains open.",
    "The critical result does not quantify the sufficiently large width threshold or establish the new depth bound at every width above target complexity.",
    "The finite representation permits arbitrary finite real weights; it does not bound their product norm or bit complexity.",
    "The learner retains the original all-input output-margin convention and exact noiseless training fit.",
    "Independent AI-agent audits and reproducible PDF builds are not Lean verification."
  ],
